%% Editable source of the "How the parts relate" diagram on /financing (docs/dao/relationship-review.md).
%% Internal: not published. The page renders the same structure as HTML (src/pages/financing.html, #structure);
%% change both together. Corrected from source/15-dao-governance-architecture.mmd (NWPT-DAO-visual-tranche-01):
%%  - milestone review no longer feeds the sponsor's clinical decisions: money pays for research work only;
%%  - sponsor, investigators, ethics committee and regulator are separate, with no shared node or hierarchy;
%%  - the private financing lane is marked proposed throughout; "bank / custody, dual control" is left out
%%    until the arrangement is agreed; the regulated investor platform (agreed route) is shown.
flowchart TB
  subgraph PUBLIC["Public information (exists now)"]
    C["Community, researchers and press"] -->|"read, ask questions, send corrections"| W["Science, evidence and updates on this website"]
    NW["No investment, payment, token or wallet function here"]
  end

  subgraph PRIVATE["Private financing (PROPOSED; only if it goes ahead)"]
    E["Eligible investors"] -->|"checked by a regulated investor platform; private legal documents"| V["Dedicated programme vehicle"]
    V -->|"records each interest in"| R["Legal register: the definitive record"]
    R -. "may be mirrored, where feasible, by" .-> M["Permissioned digital record (under evaluation)"]
    RC["If the records differ, the register controls"]
    V -->|"releases money in stages against operational milestones"| RW["Research work (paid for, not decided)"]
  end

  subgraph CLINICAL["Clinical and regulatory responsibilities (set by clinical trial law)"]
    S["Sponsor: design, dose, endpoints, safety reporting, manufacturing quality"]
    I["Investigators: conduct at each site; participants' care"]
    H["Research ethics committee: independent review"]
    G["Medicines regulator: authorisation, inspection, can stop the study"]
    SEP["Separate legal duties, not one chain of command"]
  end

  W -. "questions and corrections (no decision rights)" .-> S
